{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 133, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a skip on the first edge with a 3x3 conv gave +43/+45/+17 in the all-skip parent, versus about 0 when other edges already carry convs."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip edge to a conv helps a lot in a skip-dominated cell (+35/+32/+11), but is near zero or negative in a conv-rich cell."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a skip with a conv on edge 1 gave +35/+32/+10 in the all-skip parent, but was slightly negative in parents that already had other convs."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to a missing direct 0\u21923 edge restores the input-output path when the output is otherwise disconnected (+78/+66/+37)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an absent edge 3 with a skip reconnects the output node and gives large gains (+74/+57/+26), unlike swapping a different existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where edge 4 is absent gives a bigger gain on all three datasets (+6 to +77 in the none-edge parents) than modifying an existing conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, removing edge 3 cuts the main path to the output and drops accuracy sharply (-74/-56/-27), whereas redundant paths absorb the removal."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 is absen